    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498440": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Post Doctoral Research Associate Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Post Doctoral Research Associate Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Posting Number G/R34234P Working Title Post Doctoral Research Associate Department Franklin-Geology About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of the University of Georgia’s learning environment, advancing new knowledge, research, scholarship and creative output by faculty, students, and staff in more than 80-degree programs across 40+ units. College/Unit/Department website http://duttalab.franklinresearch.uga.edu/ Employment Type Employee Additional Schedule Information M-F, 9 am-5 pm; Evening work may be needed. Advertised Salary Commensurate with experience Anticipated Start Date 09/14/2026 Posting Date 08/06/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EOO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Laboratory Work and Wet-Laboratory Experiments: Design and conduct laboratory experiments in consultation with the PI. Sample processing and extraction; maintain accurate laboratory records; follow quality-control protocols; and troubleshoot experimental problems. Percentage of time 40 Duties/Responsibilities Instrumental Analysis and Data Interpretation: Conduct instrumental analyses using high-resolution mass spectrometry and other analytical platforms required by the project. Operate, calibrate, and perform routine maintenance of instruments; evaluate analytical quality; process and interpret data; and prepare figures and tables summarizing the results. Percentage of time 25 Duties/Responsibilities Scientific Communication, Publications, and Project Reports: Prepare peer-reviewed manuscripts, conference abstracts, presentations, project progress reports, final reports, standard operating procedures, and other scientific reports as advised by the PI. Present research findings at laboratory meetings, project meetings, and scientific conferences. Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Mentoring, Research Coordination, and Daily Laboratory Operations: Mentor and train graduate and undergraduate students in laboratory procedures, instrumental analysis, data interpretation, and responsible research practices. Coordinate daily laboratory and field activities, including sample inventories, supplies, instrument scheduling, field equipment, and research documentation. Cooperate closely with the PI, lab members, collaborators, and other project personnel. Percentage of time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Education and Outreach: Participate in project, laboratory, departmental, and community outreach activities. Assist with laboratory tours, research demonstrations, student visits, public presentations, and educational materials communicating the importance of the project. Percentage of time 5 Position Details Position Information Classification Title Post-Doctoral Associate AD FLSA Exempt UGA Job Code FTE 1.00 Minimum Qualifications Position Summary The postdoctoral researcher will lead laboratory experiments, analytical measurements, data interpretation, and computational analyses while coordinating closely with the Principal Investigator and student researchers. This position will ensure continuity across interconnected project activities, maintain rigorous quality assurance and reproducible data workflows, and accelerate completion of milestones. The postdoctoral researcher will also train and mentor graduate and undergraduate students, contribute to manuscripts and presentations, and strengthen interdisciplinary collaboration. This position is essential for timely and successful project completion. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, Certification in Position PhD required Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Strong experience in microbial ecology, geomicrobiology, and/or biogeochemistry. Proficiency in molecular biology, multi-omics workflows (primarily metagenomics and metabolomics), bioinformatics, Linux/ HPC environments, and the integration of multi-omics and geochemical datasets, with demonstrated experience using Python or R packages for statistical analyses and data visualization. Demonstrated research productivity through peer-reviewed publications, with strong scientific writing and data-presentation skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work independently, manage research responsibilities effectively, and contribute productively within a collaborative, interdisciplinary team environment. Preferred Skills: Experience with digital PCR (dPCR) and molecular workflows, including assay optimization, quantification, and analysis of low-abundance microbial targets. Experience in DNA extraction from low-biomass environmental samples and whole-metagenome sequencing data analysis, including quality control, assembly, annotation, and functional profiling. Experience with metabolomics and mass spectrometry data analysis, including processing, identification, and interpretation of metabolites from complex environmental samples. Experience in viral ecogenomics, including identification, characterization, and ecological interpretation of viral communities and virus–host interactions from metagenomic datasets. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a requirement of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Dr. Avishek Dutta Recruitment Contact Email ad28019@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Sample Publications List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
