    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/28056": {
      "title": "215 S. Jackson St.Athens, GA 30602Tel (706) 542-2222Email: hrweb@uga.edu",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Public Area Attendant Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Public Area Attendant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Tobacco use is prohibited on the University of Georgia campus and in the Georgia Center facility.\r\n\r\n**This is a temporary position that will last less than 12 months.** Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number T00240P Working Title Public Area Attendant Department PSO-Cont Ed-Aux Oper-Hotel About the University of Georgia The University of Georgia ( UGA ), a land-grant and sea-grant university with statewide commitments and responsibilities is the state’s oldest, most comprehensive, and most diversified institution of higher education ( http://www.uga.edu/ ). UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA was founded in 1785 by the Georgia General Assembly as the first state-chartered University in the country. UGA employs approximately 1,800 full-time instructional faculty and more than 7,600 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 36,000 students including over 27,500 undergraduates and over 8,500 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 17 schools and colleges, as well as a medical partnership with Augusta University housed on the UGA Health Sciences Campus in Athens. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia Center for Continuing Education & Hotel is hiring motivated, dependable, and team-orientated individuals for jobs that advance the University of Georgia’s mission of public service and outreach. The Georgia Center, located on campus across from Stegeman Coliseum, is the campus hub for the development and administration of non-credit professional and continuing education courses as well as home of the only on-campus hotel, the UGA Hotel and Conference Center. College/Unit/Department website https://www.georgiacenter.uga.edu Posting Type External Retirement Plan GDCP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Non-Benefits Eligible Full/Part time Full Time Work Schedule Work Schedule (other) 32-40 hours per week, variable hours between 6:30am to 11:00 p.m.; schedule will be set by supervisor.  Must be able to work weekends and some holidays. Advertised Salary $11.00 per hour Posting Date 07/11/2018 Open until filled Yes Closing Date Proposed Starting Date 08/13/2018 Anticipated End Date Special Instructions to Applicants Tobacco use is prohibited on the University of Georgia campus and in the Georgia Center facility. This is a temporary position that will last less than 12 months. EEO Policy Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer.  All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, gender identity, sexual orientation or protected veteran status. Location of Vacancy Athens Area Position Information Classification Title Temporary Service Worker Pay Grade 901 FLSA Non-Exempt FTE 100 Minimum Qualifications Please refer to the Additional Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification section.  Minimum qualifications may be defined by the department based on the responsibilities of the position. Preferred Qualifications Previous cleaning experience preferred Position Summary This position is responsible for ensuring that all public areas of the Georgia Center remain clean and presentable at all times. Additional Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Graduation from a standard high school, GED or any equivalent combination of training and experience. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Dependable, responsible, honest, strong work ethic, positive attitude Ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Ability to work under time constraints and in a fast-paced environment. Ability to speak and understand English. Physical Demands This is a physically demanding position. Ability to lift or move at least 30lbs. Ability to push a 50lb. cart. Ability to bend, lift, kneel, reach, and work with hands. Must be able to stand on feet and walk for long periods of time. Must be able to see dust, hair, lint and dirt. Be able to smell odors to identify the source to clean. Be attentive to detail in cleaning and presentation. Is driving required to perform essential duties outlined in this position? (This does not include infrequent trips) The successful candidate would have to provide proof that s/he has a valid driver's license when offered employment. No Does this position have financial responsibilities? No Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Clean and maintain all public areas including lobbies, hallways, entrances, vending rooms, and fitness center Percentage of time 75 Duties/Responsibilities Pick up trash and recycling in offices Percentage of time 15 Duties/Responsibilities Stock cart and storage areas with supplies Percentage of time 5 Duties/Responsibilities Participate in training sessions, departmental meetings, and other duties as assigned Percentage of time 5 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
