    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/501219": {
      "title": "215 S. Jackson St.Athens, GA 30602Tel (706) 542-2222Email: hrweb@uga.edu",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Administrative Manager Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Administrative Manager Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S15626P Working Title Administrative Manager Department PSO-VP Public Serv & Outreach About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia, a land-grant and sea-grant institution, is an international leader in outreach programming and statewide engagement. As part of UGA’s outreach mission, the division of Public Service and Outreach ( PSO ) works to help create jobs and prosperity, develop the state’s leaders, and solve critical statewide challenges. College/Unit/Department website https://outreach.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Full/Part time Full Time Work Schedule Additional Schedule Information M-F Advertised Salary Commensurate with Experience Posting Date 08/19/2026 Open until filled Yes Closing Date Proposed Starting Date 10/15/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Policy Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Information Classification Title Business Services Pro II FLSA Exempt FTE 1.00 Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a related field or equivalent and 2 years of professional experience Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of University of Georgia policies and procedures related to fiscal administration, procurement, budgeting, human resources, and general administration. Experience using University financial and human resources systems. Position Summary The Administrative Manager manages the fiscal, business, human resources, facilities, and administrative operations of the Office of the Vice President for Public Service and Outreach ( OVPPSO ). Reporting to the Senior Director of Fiscal Affairs, this position is responsible for coordinating day-to-day business operations, ensuring compliance with University policies and procedures, and serving as a primary administrative resource for OVPPSO employees. The position also provides support to the Senior Director of Fiscal Affairs by assisting with assigned division-wide reporting, information requests, recurring deadlines, strategic initiatives, special projects, and administrative process improvements across Public Service and Outreach. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Strong organizational, problem-solving, and customer service skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication. Proficient in Microsoft Excel, Microsoft Office, and University business systems. Skilled in creating reports, spreadsheets, dashboards, and tracking tools. Able to manage multiple priorities, projects, and deadlines with accuracy. Knowledge of University policies, procedures, and business practices. Exercises sound judgment and maintains confidentiality. Works effectively both independently and collaboratively with University partners. Physical Demands Standard working conditions for an office environment. Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? Yes Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Fiscal & Business Operations Manages fiscal and business activities for OVPPSO . Coordinate purchasing, travel, payroll, budget revisions, and other fiscal transactions in accordance with University and PSO policies and procedures. Monitor, reconcile, and analyze financial accounts; research and resolve discrepancies. Serve as the OVPPSO Procurement Card (P-Card) holder. Develop and maintain spreadsheets, databases, reports, and tracking tools. Serve as a resource for OVPPSO employees on fiscal, purchasing, travel, and administrative procedures. Develop and maintain standard operating procedures, process documentation, and administrative guidance. Recommend and implement process improvements to enhance efficiency, consistency, and compliance. Serve as the designated backup to the Senior Director of Fiscal Affairs for assigned fiscal and human resources transactions. Perform other related duties in support of OVPPSO business operations. Percentage of time 55 Duties/Responsibilities Administrative Operations, Strategic Initiatives & Special Projects Assists the Senior Director of Fiscal Affairs with assigned division-wide reporting, information requests, administrative activities, strategic initiatives, and special projects. Prepare reports, tracking tools, summaries, and other materials to support division-wide administrative and operational activities. Coordinate division-wide information requests, including collecting, compiling, and organizing responses; track reporting requirements and deadlines and provide status updates. Assist with division-wide strategic initiatives, administrative improvements, and special projects. Participate in assigned University and PSO committees, task forces, and working groups. Perform other related duties and special projects. Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Human Resources Administration Coordinates human resources processes for OVPPSO . Duties include but are not limited to: Coordinate position management, recruitment, hiring, onboarding, separations, and related human resources activities. Prepare and process employment actions and other human resources transactions. Maintain confidential personnel records and human resources tracking tools. Track compliance requirements, mandatory training, and onboarding activities. Serve as a resource for OVPPSO employees on human resources procedures and requirements. Percentage of time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Facilities Management Serves as Facilities Coordinator for Treanor House and Cobb House. Duties include but are not limited to: Submit and track Facilities Management Division ( FMD ) work orders and maintenance requests. Coordinate with FMD and approved vendors on maintenance, repairs, renovations, and facility improvements. Monitor custodial services and address facility-related concerns. Coordinate office moves, workspace planning, furniture and equipment installations, building access, and key assignments. Monitor building and grounds conditions and recommend improvements to support safe, functional, and efficient work environments. Serve as a Building Safety and Security Representative. Percentage of time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Professional Development Maintains the knowledge and skills needed to perform the position effectively. Complete training and professional development activities related to assigned responsibilities. Maintain proficiency in University business systems, Microsoft Office applications, reporting tools, and other relevant technology. Stay current on University policies, procedures, regulations, and administrative best practices. Apply new knowledge and skills to improve business operations, administrative processes, and efficiency. Percentage of time 5 Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Anjali Dougherty Recruitment Contact Email adougher@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503897": {
      "title": "215 S. Jackson St.Athens, GA 30602Tel (706) 542-2222Email: hrweb@uga.edu",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Materials Handler I Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Materials Handler I Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S15686P Working Title Materials Handler I Department VetMed-VTH Warehouse About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia College of Veterinary Medicine, founded in 1946, is dedicated to training future veterinarians, providing services to animal owners and veterinarians, and conducting investigations to improve the health of animals as well as people. The college benefits pets and their owners, food-producing animals, and wildlife by offering the highest quality hospital and diagnostic laboratory services. Equipped with the most technologically advanced facilities located on a university campus, the college is dedicated to safeguarding public health by studying emerging infectious diseases that affect both animal and human health. The College of Veterinary Medicine values all members of the university community, recognizing that differences in experience and culture can only lead to a more well-rounded, accepting academic environment as embodied in our Principles of Community (<a href=“”http://vet.uga.edu/principles-of-community/“> http://vet.uga.edu/principles-of-community/ ” target=“_blank”> http://vet.uga.edu/principles-of-community/</a >) College/Unit/Department website https://vet.uga.edu/hospital-and-primary-care/hospital/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Full/Part time Full Time Work Schedule Additional Schedule Information Business Hours- Monday to Friday, 8am-5pm Advertised Salary $16.92-$18 per hour Posting Date 09/01/2026 Open until filled Yes Closing Date Proposed Starting Date 10/11/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Policy Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Information Classification Title Materials Handler I FLSA Non-Exempt FTE 1.00 Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications -Experience working in a warehouse setting utilizing hand truck, pallet jack, maintaining inventory counts Position Summary Performs manual and clerical duties related to receiving, inspecting, and stocking: Receives shipments and checks for accuracy against purchase orders; Stocks inventory shelves by the appropriate hospital inventory numbers; Pulls inventory for various departments within the teaching hospital; Assist in the ordering, receiving, distributing and taking inventory of compressed gases for the hospital. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Basic computer and arithmetic skills. Skills in operating automotive, materials handling, and office equipment. Detail-oriented, observant, and safety conscious. Physical Demands Lift, and carry up to 75 pounds. Sit, stand, stoop, bend and walk intermittently during the day on hard floor surfaces. Manual dexterity sufficient to accurately work with small, delicate pieces of equipment or large heavy objects/containers/machinery. Work for long periods of time with arms extended. Driving to perform job related duties. Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Receives all deliveries to VMC and checks for accuracy/discrepancies against purchase orders. Percentage of time 25 Duties/Responsibilities Stocks inventory shelves by the appropriate hospital inventory numbers. Percentage of time 25 Duties/Responsibilities Pulls inventory for various departments within the teaching hospital. Percentage of time 25 Duties/Responsibilities Assist as needed with the stocking of hospital Cubex machines. Percentage of time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Data entry in hospital VetView system. Sorts all incoming mail for the Vet Med Center, which includes all departments, housed on this campus. Percentage of time 15 Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Kris Mitchell Recruitment Contact Email krista.mitchell@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
