formats. Percentage of time 40 Position Details Position Information Classification Title Temporary Hourly Professional FLSA Non-Exempt UGA Job Code FTE .72500 Minimum Qualifications Position Summary The University of Georgia Athletic Association is seeking a passionate and driven individual for a full-time post-graduate internship within the Creative Services team. This position offers hands-on experience producing high-impact video content that supports the UGA Athletics brand through storytelling, fan engagement, and recruiting efforts across digital and social platforms. The ideal candidate is a visual storyteller who thrives in fast-paced environments, understands the college sports landscape, and is eager to contribute creatively within a collaborative team. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, Certification in Position Bachelor’s degree or 2 years of applicable experience in video production, content creation, or a related field. Previous experience working in a collegiate or professional sports creative setting. Portfolio or demo reel showcasing relevant creative video work (please include with application). Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Proficiency in Adobe Premiere Pro; working knowledge of After Effects and Photoshop preferred. Experience with video production, including lighting, audio, and DSLR , mirrorless, or cinema camera operation. Understanding social media trends and platforms, especially related to sports content. Ability to work flexible hours, including nights, weekends, and holidays. Excellent time management, communication, and teamwork skills. Physical Demands Normal working conditions of an office environment. Driving. Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a requirement of this position? Yes Does this position have direct