      "description": "University of Georgia | FoodPro Assistant Manager Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits FoodPro Assistant Manager Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S15240P Working Title FoodPro Assistant Manager Department Auxiliary Central Storage About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website dining.uga.edu Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Full/Part time Full Time Work Schedule Additional Schedule Information This position offers a 40 hour work week. Hours and schedule may vary and will include evenings and weekends. Advertised Salary 19.907692 Posting Date 06/02/2026 Open until filled Yes Closing Date Proposed Starting Date 06/15/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Policy Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Information Classification Title Inventory Assistant I FLSA Non-Exempt FTE 1.00 Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications Position Summary Reporting to the FoodPro Manager, the primary function of the FoodPro Assistant Manager will be to perform daily invoice entry and product maintenance within FoodPro. Under the supervision of the FoodPro Manager, the FoodPro Assistant Manager will also provide support and guidance to units on daily activities needed for inventory and invoicing. These include developing/maintaining SOPs for receiving product from external vendors, transferring goods between Dining locations, taking weekly inventory and report analysis to ensure all units are operating at the highest level for current and future fiscal and production weeks. Responsibilities also include serving as the back-up to the FoodPro Manager. Will also serve as backup for POS Manager as needed. Provide training and support to all units on the process of receiving goods to and/or from respective units. Work with user to ensure procedures are followed in the use of FoodPro. Work to establish inventory, schedule cycle, and special event menus. Work to promote the use and enhance the FoodPro program. Work with Dining Service staff in all areas to ensure procedures are followed in the use of FoodPro. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Extremely well-organized with strong analytical skills; attention to detail. Able to accurately maintain a variety of records and to prepare reports. Able to meet deadlines and manage time accordingly. Able to strategically plan and logistically execute work flows. Ability to successfully manage through crisis and extenuating circumstances. Well-versed at building relationships internally and be a consummate team player. Able to work autonomously, with little supervision, and effectively to troubleshoot challenges as they arise. Able to work varied shifts including evenings and weekends. Present a professional image and be able to work collegially and effectively within a community of students, employees, faculty, staff and others. Possess a high degree of integrity, ethics, and dedication to the mission of the University of Georgia. Physical Demands Regularly sit, and occasionally needed to stand/walk. Frequently lift and/or move 20 lbs. to 50 lbs. Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Accurate invoice entry into FoodPro. Review of scanned invoices and EDI from locations to ensure catchall numbers are identified and resolved through communication with Dining Hall staff. Monitor credits indicated on invoices vs. credits claimed on vendor payment portal. Enter credit memos into FoodPro. Audit and verify inventory counts and procedures on predetermined rotation cycle. May be conducted in person or through forensic examination of product credits vs purchases vs amount on hand. Monitor Location Cost Summary and Inventory Analysis weekly reporting. Investigate issues that may be causing report anomalies. Create inventory numbers and add them to the relevant FoodPro locations with correct inventory and purchase units and pack ratios per requests from TeamDynamix Ticket system. Also, to include all pertinent information of items including but not limited to its vendor order number(s), brand information, UPC , etc. Communicate all new inventory information to the Associate Director for Culinary Development/Certified Executive Chef, Nutrition team, POS Manager, FoodPro Manager and production team (unit production managers, sous chefs, and material handlers). Report issues or irregularities to FoodPro Manager and Executive Chef. Percentage of time 70 Duties/Responsibilities Serve as back-up to FoodPro Manager and Point-of-Sale manager. Assist with FoodPro duties and special projects as needed. Routine duties include product additions, user support, client software installation and weekly start-up/production run. Special projects varied but may include projects requiring multiple steps, complex processes and multiple team players. Provide training and support to all units on the process of receiving goods to and/or from respective units. Work with user to ensure procedures are followed in the use of FoodPro. Work to establish inventory, schedule cycle, and special event menus. Work to promote the use and enhance the FoodPro program. Work with Dining Service staff in all areas to ensure procedures are followed in the use of FoodPro. Percentage of time 15 Duties/Responsibilities Maintains Master List Management software for Prime Vendor ordering. Troubleshoot out of stock items by consistently monitoring changes to discontinued products and make appropriate changes/associations in MLM software and FoodPro, ensuring products are ordered and invoiced properly. Communicate with Prime Vendor Account rep and Executive Chef as needed to stay ahead of pending changes to products. Percentage of time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Represents the department internally as needed at committee meetings and campus events and externally at related food service organization meetings/events and community events. Perform other duties and assist in operating units as assigned. Percentage of time 5 Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Brian Gibbs Recruitment Contact Email bggibbs@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to bend, stoop, squat, kneel, stand, climb stairs, and work with hands above head frequently and work on a standard and/or extended ladder throughout a work shift? Yes No No Response * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * How did you hear about this job opportunity? UGAjobsearch.com InsideHigherEd.com Indeed.com hCareers.com LinkedIn Facebook The Department of Labor Goodwill UGA Employee Other Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Cover Letter Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
