    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/490462": {
      "title": "215 S. Jackson St.Athens, GA 30602Tel (706) 542-2222Email: hrweb@uga.edu",
      "description": "University of Georgia | AI Research Facilitator Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits AI Research Facilitator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please provide name and contact information for three professional references This is a full-time, on-site position This position is not eligible for work authorization sponsorship Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S15371P Working Title AI Research Facilitator Department EITS-Research Computing About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website gacrc.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Full/Part time Full Time Work Schedule Additional Schedule Information 8am – 5pm; Monday – Friday Advertised Salary Up to 92,000 Posting Date 06/26/2026 Open until filled Yes Closing Date Proposed Starting Date 08/03/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please provide name and contact information for three professional references This is a full-time, on-site position This position is not eligible for work authorization sponsorship Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Policy Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Information Classification Title Research Computing Pro III FLSA Exempt FTE 1.00 Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a related field or equivalent and 5 years of professional experience Preferred Qualifications Applied or research experience supporting AI computational workflows in academic research environments. Familiarity with HPC job schedulers (e.g., Slurm), containerized computing environments, and data management workflows. Prior experience delivering research training, workshops, or consultation services. Master’s or Ph.D. in computer science, data science, or a research domain with significant AI experience. Four or more years of progressive experience implementing and supporting AI/ML workflows, including hands-on model development, data preparation, and optimization in research or industry settings. Position Summary The Georgia Advanced Computing Resource Center ( GACRC ), a division of Enterprise Information Technology Services at the University of Georgia, seeks to establish an AI Research Facilitator position to support the University’s rapidly expanding needs in artificial intelligence and data-driven research. The GACRC provides advanced computing and research storage services to more than 500 research groups, and recent multimillion-dollar investments in GPU -accelerated infrastructure have positioned UGA to support leading-edge AI research across disciplines. Over the past three years, the University has undertaken the Presidential Interdisciplinary Faculty Hiring Initiative in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence, bringing approximately 70 new faculty hires to campus. At the same time, existing faculty across the sciences, social sciences, humanities, arts, and professional programs are increasingly incorporating AI and machine learning into their research portfolios. To fully realize the potential of these rapidly growing AI-driven initiatives, UGA must provide specialized, human-centered research support that complements its advanced computing investments. The AI Research Facilitator will play a central role in enabling faculty to effectively leverage AI methodologies, accelerating research impact across the institution. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Demonstrated expertise using modern AI/ML frameworks (e.g., PyTorch, TensorFlow, Scikit-learn). Deep understanding of large language models (LLMs), including model architectures, training and fine-tuning approaches, inference pipelines, and responsible use in research contexts. Proficiency in Python, R, CUDA , or other languages common in AI research. Experience working with GPU -accelerated computing resources, preferably within an HPC environment. Experience preparing, managing, and curating datasets for machine learning workflows. Ability to translate faculty research goals into appropriate AI methods, models, and computational strategies. Working knowledge of ethical AI principles, bias mitigation, and reproducibility practices. Strong communication skills, including experience developing workshops, training materials, or documentation for varied audiences. Demonstrated ability to work effectively in collaborative, interdisciplinary research environments. Physical Demands Normal office environment Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities AI Research Support and Consultation Provide hands-on consultation to faculty and graduate students integrating AI, machine learning, or data-intensive methods into their research workflows. Assist with data preparation, model development, training optimization, and performance tuning on GPU -accelerated systems. Offer tailored, high-engagement guidance to new AI-focused faculty as well as existing researchers expanding into AI-driven approaches. Percentage of time 40 Duties/Responsibilities Training, Outreach, and Community Building Develop workshops, online training modules, and documentation to broaden AI skills and best practices across campus. Support interdisciplinary collaborations by connecting researchers with shared computational approaches. Engage departments adopting AI for the first time to ensure sustainable and responsible integration of AI tools into research and teaching. Percentage of time 30 Duties/Responsibilities Coordination and Institutional Alignment Work closely with GACRC and EITS leadership, the Office of Research, the Institute for AI, and academic units to ensure services align with evolving research needs. Provide input to help guide institutional strategy for AI computing, workflows, and research support. Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Technology Monitoring and Evaluation Stay current with emerging AI frameworks, workflows, tools, and best practices. Assess new technologies and their potential to improve research productivity or strengthen UGA’s AI research capabilities. Percentage of time 10 Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Dr. Guy Cormier Recruitment Contact Email gcormier@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Sample Publications List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478493": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Hort Rubio-Ames PhD Grad Student Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Hort Rubio-Ames PhD Grad Student Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Posting Number G/R16123P Working Title Hort Rubio-Ames PhD Grad Student Department CAES-Horticulture About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department Our department specializes in a multitude of research areas and works on a vast array of fruit, vegetables, ornamentals, endangered native species and row crops. Our diversity is one of our greatest strengths. College/Unit/Department website https://hort.caes.uga.edu/ Employment Type Employee Additional Schedule Information Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 06/01/2022 Posting Date 01/25/2022 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Tifton Area EOO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Duties/Responsibilities Position Details Position Information Classification Title Graduate Research Assistant FLSA Exempt UGA Job Code FTE .325 Minimum Qualifications Position Summary The Small Fruit Research and Extension Lab is seeking a resourceful and motivated individual interested in Horticulture, especially blueberry production and management to fill 1 PhD research assistantship in the Department of Horticulture at the University of Georgia’s Tifton campus.  Potential research topics are flexible but will have a general focus on blueberry production and cultural management practices (fertilization, pruning, and water management), and alternative blueberry production systems. The candidate chosen for the position will have the opportunity to cultivate the necessary skills in the field as well as gain outreach and extension experiences, and overall professional development relevant to future careers in the industry and academia. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, Certification in Position Experience in plant physiology and research Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Agronomy, horticulture, plant physiology, or a related discipline from an accredited institution is preferred . Additionally, previous field and work experience relevant to the potential research topics is preferred. A good understanding of project design, data entry, statistical analysis, and technical writing is preferred. Interested candidates should be open to learning new skills, have a positive attitude, and a strong work ethic. A willingness to work outdoors in the heat and humidity is preferred. Physical Demands Bending, lifting up to fifty pounds, working outdoors in varying weather conditions Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a requirement of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. For assistance with your application or login, please email hrweb@uga.edu. Recruitment Contact Name Zilfina Rubio-Ames Recruitment Contact Email Zilfina.Rubio-Ames@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Optional Documents Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/495627": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant to the Vice Provosts",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Administrative Assistant to the Vice Provosts Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Administrative Assistant to the Vice Provosts Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S15504P Working Title Administrative Assistant to the Vice Provosts Department SRVPAA-SR VP Acad Affrs & Prov About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Full/Part time Full Time Work Schedule Additional Schedule Information 8 am – 5 pm, M-F Advertised Salary Up to $55,000 Posting Date 07/24/2026 Open until filled Yes Closing Date Proposed Starting Date 09/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Policy Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Information Classification Title Executive Assistant I FLSA Non-Exempt FTE 1.00 Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or equivalent Preferred Qualifications Position Summary This position provides administrative support to the Office of the Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost and serves as an integral member of the staff support team. The position provides primary administrative support for the Vice Provost for Academic Affairs and the Vice Provost for Academic and Community Engagement. Working collaboratively with other staff, this position helps ensure efficient and effective service delivery within the Provost’s Office. The position routinely handles confidential matters and must exercise sound judgment, discretion, and professionalism. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies The successful candidate will demonstrate: Strong organizational, written, and oral communication skills. Demonstrated ability to provide professional administrative support in a fast-paced, executive-level office. Ability to manage multiple priorities, solve problems, and follow through on time-sensitive assignments. Ability to work independently, ask appropriate questions, and collaborate as part of a team. Strong attention to detail and ability to proofread and prepare accurate documents. Proficiency with Microsoft Office, including Outlook calendar management, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Teams. Demonstrated ability to exercise discretion and sound judgment with confidential information. Physical Demands Normal office functions, including: * Walking short distances on the UGA campus to pick up and deliver time-sensitive items; * Lifting/carrying boxes of approximately 15-20 pounds; * Bending, lifting, and stooping for filing. Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Executive Administrative Support and Calendar Management Support the Vice Provost for Academic Affairs and the Vice Provost for Academic and Community Engagement through proactive calendar management, meeting coordination, preparation of materials, and coordination of logistics. Serve as a primary point of contact for scheduling and help ensure that meetings, materials, and follow-up items are organized and timely. Percentage of time 40 Duties/Responsibilities Office Operations and Communication Provide general administrative support for the Provost’s Office, including greeting visitors, answering calls, monitoring incoming mail and email, responding to routine inquiries, routing requests appropriately, proofreading and transmitting outgoing documents, and communicating information about university procedures, policies, regulations, and programs. Percentage of time 30 Duties/Responsibilities Financial, Records, and Document Management Process routine financial transactions, including reimbursements, office supply orders, and state and foundation check requests. Maintain physical and electronic filing systems, scan and organize records, and archive materials in accordance with university policies. Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Financial, Records, and Document Management Maintains the Provost’s Office filing system. Handles all hard copy filing and scanning of digitally filed documents. Keeps documents, mail, correspondence, and other materials organized in a system that is easily accessible to all staff. Annually archives materials in accordance with University policies. Percentage of time 10 Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Jasmyne Willingham Recruitment Contact Email jasmyne.willingham@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
