    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478417": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Temporary Painter - FMD Griffin Campus Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Temporary Painter - FMD Griffin Campus Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Posting Number G/R27496P Working Title Temporary Painter - FMD Griffin Campus Department CAES-Griffin Campus About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Employment Type Employee Additional Schedule Information Monday – Friday; 8am-5pm Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 10/22/2024 Posting Date 10/08/2024 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Griffin Area EOO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Prepare walls and other surfaces for painting by scraping using sandpaper, removing old paint, etc. Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Fill cracks and holes with appropriate material. Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Clean and prep all materials for painting. Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Apply paint by spraying and/or rolling and/or using a brush. Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Assist other skilled tradesmen and perform related work as required. Percentage of time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Move furniture and operate forklift and mobile platform. Percentage of time 10 Position Details Position Information Classification Title Temporary Skilled Crafts/Trades FLSA Non-Exempt UGA Job Code FTE 1.00 Minimum Qualifications Position Summary This position is responsible for preparation and paint related work on Campus facilities including determining painting needs, color blending and matching and sequences of painting operations and method. Employee functions will include maintaining tool and equipment, paint stock and proper paint disposal. Assignments are received in writing and orally and work is performed under general direction from supervisor. Work is reviewed through inspection while in progress and upon completion. The position will be required to perform other functions related to the general activities in facilities operation and maintenance. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, Certification in Position Candidate will have verifiable skills as a painter. Candidate will understand paint required for various applications both interior and exterior. Candidate will have knowledge of equipment required for paint preparation and application. Candidate will have knowledge of methods of equipment maintenance. Candidate will have general knowledge of use of hand and power tools related to general facility maintenance, upkeep and repair. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Thorough knowledge of the standard methods, equipment, materials, tools and practices of the painting trade. Considerable knowledge of the hazards and safety precautions of the trade. Ability to successfully manage hazardous waste satellite facility. Ability to communicate clearly and concisely in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees and university personnel. Skilled in the use of standard tools and equipment of the trade. Ability to lift and carry 45 pounds. Physical Demands Use hands to reach and handle tools and objects; climb ladders and scaffolds; work from heights; lift up to 40 pounds; drive fork lift and vehicles. Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a requirement of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Dale Hess Recruitment Contact Email dhess@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone 770-228-7225 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Optional Documents List of References with Contact Information Cover Letter Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
