    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/494929": {
      "title": "Associate Director, EPOMBA Alumni Engagement & Rankings",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Director, EPOMBA Alumni Engagement &amp; Rankings Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Director, EPOMBA Alumni Engagement & Rankings Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S15476P Working Title Associate Director, EPOMBA Alumni Engagement & Rankings Department Terry-Exec/Prof MBA About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Full/Part time Full Time Work Schedule Additional Schedule Information Typically, Monday through Friday 8:00 am – 5:00 pm Advertised Salary $58,000 + commensurate with experience Posting Date 07/21/2026 Open until filled Yes Closing Date Proposed Starting Date 09/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Atlanta Area EEO Policy Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Information Classification Title Alumni Relations Officer II FLSA Exempt FTE 1.00 Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a related field or equivalent and 2 years of professional experience Preferred Qualifications Position Summary The Executive, Professional and Online EPOMBA Program office seeks an Associate Director of EPOMBA Alumni Engagement & Rankings to lead a high-impact function at the intersection of alumni relations, data strategy, and global rankings performance. This role is responsible for building lifelong relationships with EPOMBA graduates while designing and executing a data-driven strategy that strengthens the school’s position in leading EPOMBA rankings (Financial Times, QS, U.S. News & World Report, Bloomberg Businessweek). This is a highly visible, cross-functional leadership role that connects alumni engagement directly to institutional reputation, requiring both strategic thinking and operational excellence. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Ability to lead cross-functional initiatives and manage complex projects Strong analytical skills with experience working with large datasets and reporting tools Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills Knowledge of EPOMBA rankings methodologies (Financial Times, QS, U.S. News, Bloomberg) Knowledge of CRM systems (e.g., GAIL , SLATE ) and analytics tools (Tableau, Power BI) Physical Demands Working in a normal office environment. Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Alumni Engagement Strategy & Leadership: Design and lead a comprehensive EPOMBA alumni engagement strategy Oversee alumni communications, digital platforms, and engagement campaigns to drive participation and connection Build and support regional alumni chapters and volunteer leadership structures Serve as a point of contact for alumni relations within the EPOMBA program Percentage of time 25 Duties/Responsibilities Rankings Strategy & Execution: Own end-to-end coordination of EPOMBA rankings submissions, with a focus on alumni-driven metrics Develop and execute strategies to improve survey response rates, data quality, and alumni participation Translate rankings methodologies into actionable engagement and data collection plans Partner across EPOMBA to align rankings strategy with program priorities Percentage of time 25 Duties/Responsibilities Alumni Data & Analytics: Lead the design and administration of alumni surveys capturing career outcomes, satisfaction, and program impact Oversee data integrity across CRM systems, survey tools, and reporting platforms Build dashboards and reports tracking key rankings metrics (salary growth, career progression, alumni satisfaction) Generate insights and recommendations to inform program improvements and rankings positioning Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Events & Programming Oversight: Oversee the planning and execution of high-impact alumni events (reunions, networking, thought leadership) Ensure programming aligns with engagement and data collection goals Evaluate event effectiveness using participation and feedback data Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Cross-Functional Leadership: Collaborate closely with EPOMBA Career Management to track employment outcomes and alumni career trajectories Partner with Institutional Research on data governance and reporting standards Work with TDAR to align engagement with fundraising strategies Coordinate with Marketing & Communications to amplify alumni success stories Percentage of time 10 Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Susan Brown Recruitment Contact Email susan.brown@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this vacant position? \r\n(UGA Jobs -UGA's Job Board, LinkedIn, Indeed.com, Inside HigherEdJobs, UGA Staff Listserv, Terry College Listserv, a current UGA Employee, other - please provide resource) (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/CV List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
