    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/480446": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Animal Caretaker Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Animal Caretaker Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Posting Number G/R32995P Working Title Animal Caretaker Department VetMed-VTH Large Animal Hosp About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia College of Veterinary Medicine, founded in 1946, is dedicated to training future veterinarians, providing services to animal owners and veterinarians, and conducting investigations to improve the health of animals as well as people. The college benefits pets and their owners, food-producing animals, and wildlife by offering the highest quality hospital and diagnostic laboratory services. Equipped with the most technologically advanced facilities located on a university campus, the college is dedicated to safeguarding public health by studying emerging infectious diseases that affect both animal and human health. The College of Veterinary Medicine values all members of the university community, recognizing that differences in experience and culture can only lead to a more well-rounded, accepting academic environment as embodied in our Principles of Community (<a href=“”http://vet.uga.edu/principles-of-community/“> http://vet.uga.edu/principles-of-community/ ” target=“_blank”> http://vet.uga.edu/principles-of-community/</a >) College/Unit/Department website https://vet.uga.edu/hospital-and-primary-care/hospital/ Employment Type Employee Additional Schedule Information Varied hours that support the unit. The hospital is a 24/7/365 operations.  Weekend and holiday shifts expected. Advertised Salary 12.75 per hour Anticipated Start Date 05/24/2026 Posting Date 04/30/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EOO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Removing manure and soiled shavings/bedding in patient stalls and kennels. Clean and disinfect discharged patient stalls. Prepare new patient stalls as directed by  Supervisor. Percentage of time 75 Duties/Responsibilities Clean and maintain large animal areas on a regular basis by sweeping, vacuuming and hose clean. Percentage of time 15 Duties/Responsibilities Assists DVM’s, Technicians and Students when appropriate and requested. Percentage of time 10 Position Details Position Information Classification Title Student Assistant FLSA Non-Exempt UGA Job Code FTE .49 Minimum Qualifications Position Summary This work involves the cleaning and maintenance of patient facilities in the Vet Teaching Hospital. This includes: 1. Removing manure and soiled shavings/bedding in patient stalls and kennels. 2. Cleaning and disinfecting discharged patient stalls. 3. In specific areas of the hospital, floors are swept, vacuumed and hosed clean. 4. New patient stalls are prepared as directed by Lead Caretaker or Supervisor. 5. Various other facilities of the hospital in both large and small animal are also cleaned and maintained on a regular basis. 6. Assistance is also given to DVM’s, Technicians and Students where appropriate and requested. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, Certification in Position Preferred experience working around large animals, manure, and medical equipment Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Comfortable in handling, cleaning and working in close proximity with small and large animals. Physical Demands - Lift and carry up to 75 pounds. - Sit, stand, stoop, bend intermittently during the day on hard floor surfaces. - Work for long periods of time with arms extended. - Work with cleaning solutions and strong animal odors. - Wear of protective gear including mask, gloves, gown, hairnet, safety goggles, etc. Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a requirement of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Drew Clements Recruitment Contact Email Drew.clements2@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone 7065424459 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478378": {
      "title": "Temporary Variety Testing Assistant",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Temporary Variety Testing Assistant - Mailhot Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Temporary Variety Testing Assistant - Mailhot Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Details Posting Number G/R19323P Working Title Temporary Variety Testing Assistant - Mailhot Department CAES-Crop & Soil Sciences About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Employment Type Employee Additional Schedule Information Monday-Friday; work hours will vary. Advertised Salary $12.75 Anticipated Start Date 09/19/2022 Posting Date 09/12/2022 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Griffin Area EOO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Supporting seed lab activities including inventory, packaging, quality evaluations and ginning of cotton samples. Percentage of time 60 Duties/Responsibilities Supporting field activities including planting, data collection, and harvest. Percentage of time 30 Duties/Responsibilities Cleaning of workspace and state vehicles. Percentage of time 10 Position Details Position Information Classification Title Temporary Technical Paraprofessional FLSA Non-Exempt UGA Job Code FTE 0.50 Minimum Qualifications Position Summary This is a part-time (up to 20 hours per week) position. The assistant will be working in the Variety Testing program, performing seed lab activities and sometimes field work. This position will report to Daniel Mailhot, Program Director. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, Certification in Position High School Graduate. Contact Daniel Mailhot at daniel.mailhot@uga.edu for a review of qualifications prior to applying. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Good time management skills. Ability to remain productively engaged in work activities. Physical Demands Driving. Occasionally lift 30-lb bags, sitting, standing, reaching, pulling, bending and walking. Tolerance of outdoor working conditions including sun, heat, humidity, insects, and potentially dust. Indoor exposures include dust and potentially noise. *Includes some exposure to peanut and wheat allergens. * Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a requirement of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Daniel Mailhot Recruitment Contact Email daniel.mailhot@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
