    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/497030": {
      "title": "215 S. Jackson St.Athens, GA 30602Tel (706) 542-2222Email: hrweb@uga.edu",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Development and Alumni Communications Professional Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Development and Alumni Communications Professional Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S15533P Working Title Development and Alumni Communications Professional Department Franklin-Deans Communications About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of the University of Georgia’s learning environment, advancing new knowledge, research, scholarship and creative output by faculty, students, and staff in more than 80-degree programs across 40+ units. College/Unit/Department website https://franklin.uga.edu Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Full/Part time Full Time Work Schedule Additional Schedule Information M-F, 8am-5pm; Evening or weekend work may be required Advertised Salary Commensurate with experience Posting Date 07/30/2026 Open until filled Yes Closing Date Proposed Starting Date 09/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Policy Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Information Classification Title Communications Pro II FLSA Exempt FTE 1.00 Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a related field or equivalent and 2 years of professional experience Preferred Qualifications Position Summary The Development and Alumni Communications Professional supports Franklin College of Arts and Sciences’ communications efforts related to development, alumni relations, donor engagement and college newsletters. This position works as part of the Franklin College marketing and communications team and collaborates with Franklin Development and Alumni Relations, academic departments, school and institute communicators, central Development and Alumni Relations, central Marketing and Communications, and other university partners. The position helps identify, develop and coordinate alumni, donor, faculty, student, research and department-level stories for use in development communications, alumni engagement, newsletters, websites, solicitations, event communications, stewardship materials and related college channels. The role requires strong writing and editing skills, sound editorial judgment, project coordination, attention to detail and the ability to adapt content for different audiences and purposes. As the DAR communications point of contact within Franklin MarCom, this position participates in content planning discussions and helps recognize opportunities to use stories across multiple channels. For example, the position may identify that a research story could support an upcoming donor solicitation, that an alumni conversation could become a department web profile, or that a faculty or student achievement could be used in a newsletter, web story or advancement communication. The position coordinates newsletter content and related workflows, drafts and edits alumni and donor communications, supports annual giving and stewardship communications, and helps ensure projects are accurate, timely, audience-appropriate and aligned with college and university standards. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Bachelor’s degree in communications, journalism, marketing, public relations, English or a related field, or equivalent combination of education and experience, and 2 years of professional experience in communications, marketing, advancement communications, alumni communications, development communications, editorial work, content development or related work. Physical Demands Work is primarily performed in an office or hybrid office environment. Some evening and weekend work may be required for college, alumni, donor or university events. Occasional travel to meetings, events or off-campus activities may be required. Ability to lift or move light event or communications materials up to 25 pounds. Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Support development and alumni communications planning and content coordination Serve as a communications point of contact for assigned development and alumni relations projects within Franklin College. Identify, develop and coordinate stories, alumni profiles, donor impact narratives, faculty/research highlights, student success stories and department-level content for use across DAR , MarCom, newsletters, websites, events, social media, solicitations and related channels. Participate in Franklin MarCom content planning meetings and help identify how upcoming stories, faculty work, alumni relationships and department priorities may support donor communications, alumni engagement and college communications goals. Work with Franklin DAR staff, major gift officers, donor relations, alumni relations, academic departments and central university partners to support annual giving, stewardship, alumni engagement and related communications priorities. Translate academic, research, donor and alumni information into clear, compelling and audience-centered communications. Maintain awareness of upcoming solicitations, campaigns, events, donor priorities, alumni opportunities and department needs to identify timely communications opportunities. Percentage of time 30 Duties/Responsibilities Coordinate Franklin College newsletter workflows and content calendars Coordinate assigned newsletter workflows in collaboration with the Franklin MarCom team, Franklin DAR , departments, schools, institutes and central university partners. Maintain newsletter calendars, production timelines, content trackers, review steps and related workflow documents. Gather and organize newsletter content from academic departments, DAR partners, faculty, staff and MarCom colleagues. Review newsletter requests and work with supervisor and team members to determine appropriate timing, audience, channel and content approach. Identify opportunities to reduce duplication, improve consistency and align newsletter content with college priorities. Coordinate newsletter content across alumni, donor, department, faculty, staff, student and external audiences as assigned. Coordinate with part-time, student, freelance, vendor or shared communications support assisting with newsletter production. Review available newsletter and email performance data and share observations or recommendations with supervisor. Percentage of time 25 Duties/Responsibilities Develop and coordinate alumni, donor and advancement communications Write, edit and coordinate alumni profiles, donor impact stories, stewardship content, solicitation copy, campaign updates, event communications, invitations, web content, newsletter items and related DAR materials. Support major college and university advancement initiatives, including annual giving campaigns, donor stewardship efforts, alumni engagement campaigns, fundraising priorities and signature DAR events. Draft and update assigned advancement communications materials, including donor impact stories, solicitation language, alumni profiles, event communications, newsletter content and web copy. Coordinate with designers, photographers, videographers, freelancers, vendors or other MarCom colleagues to support written, visual and multimedia materials. Ensure communications are accurate, timely, brand-aligned, audience-appropriate and consistent with university and college standards. Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Serve as a communications contact between Franklin MarCom, DAR and academic units Serve as a communications contact for Franklin College DAR within the Franklin MarCom team. Build and maintain strong working relationships with development officers, alumni relations staff, department heads, school and institute communicators, faculty, central DAR and central MarCom. Share communications opportunities, story ideas, channel considerations, audience needs and message recommendations with supervisor and project partners. Help departments identify how alumni, donor, faculty, student and research stories can support web content, newsletters, engagement, solicitations and related communications needs. Coordinate communications timelines and expectations across multiple stakeholders to help projects move efficiently from idea to publication or delivery. Percentage of time 15 Duties/Responsibilities Support communications processes and standards Support improvements to DAR and newsletter communications processes, templates, workflows, calendars, intake systems and review practices. Follow established standards for alumni profiles, donor impact stories, newsletters, event communications and solicitation-related content. Support Franklin MarCom efforts to improve content planning, editorial consistency, brand alignment and project coordination. Use project tracking tools and shared planning systems to document work, manage deadlines and improve transparency. Percentage of time 5 Duties/Responsibilities Other duties as assigned Support other Franklin College communications, marketing, alumni, donor, event or reputational priorities as assigned. Assist with urgent communications needs, leadership requests, event support or cross-functional college projects when needed. Percentage of time 5 Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Kyle Martin Recruitment Contact Email Kyle.Martin5@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
