ligibility Benefits Eligible Full/Part time Full Time Work Schedule Additional Schedule Information Monday-Friday, 8am-5pm Advertised Salary $43,000-48,000 Posting Date 08/13/2026 Open until filled Yes Closing Date Proposed Starting Date 11/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Policy Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Information Classification Title Digital Content Pro I FLSA Exempt FTE 1.00 Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a related field or equivalent Preferred Qualifications Position Summary The Digital Coordinator is responsible for expanding the organization’s reach, relevance, and impact across digital platforms while strengthening audience habits and engagement. This position serves as the primary driver of digital storytelling, content distribution, audience development, and digital product growth, ensuring that the organization’s journalism and programming reach audiences where they increasingly consume media. The role focuses on attracting and retaining new listeners and supporters, increasing daily engagement through newsletters, podcasts, social media, photo, video, and web content. Working collaboratively with newsroom, programming, and central Marketing & Communications staff, this position creates and repurposes existing content into compelling digital experiences that execute strategic opportunities for audience growth. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Physical Demands Standard office environment Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Digital Content Production & Storytelling Produce, shoot, edit, and publish vertical and horizontal video content for social media, website, podcasts, and other digital platforms. Create visual companion content for feature stories, interviews, and special projects. Capture photography and visual assets to support digital news stories and audience engagement efforts. Repurpose broadcast and newsroom content into engaging digital formats. Pitch, develop, and execute original digital storytelling initiatives. Identify innovative ways to extend the reach and impact of existing programming through digital channels Percentage of time 25 Duties/Responsibilities Newsletter & Audience Habit Development Curate and produce a daily email newsletter featuring news, features, and organizational content. Develop newsletter strategies that increase open rates, engagement, and audience retention. Develop strategies to increase newsletter subscriptions Create audience engagement initiatives that encourage daily interaction with organizational content. Support strategies that strengthen audience loyalty and build future donor pipelines. Monitor newsletter performance metrics and recommend improvements. Percentage of time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Podcast Production & Development Collaborate with programming staff to produce and distribute a daily news podcast. Manage and maintain existing podcast offerings, including publishing schedules and platform distribution. Assist in developing new podcast concepts, series, and segments. Monitor podcast performance and audience trends to support growth initiatives. Ensure podcast content aligns with organizational goals and audience development strategies. Percentage of time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Social Media Management & Audience Growth Manage and update social media platforms with timely news, programming highlights, and audience engagement content. Develop and execute strategies to increase digital reach, audience growth, and brand awareness. Create platform-specific content that supports audience acquisition and retention. Monitor social media analytics and adjust content strategies based on performance. Engage with audiences and identify emerging digital trends and opportunities. Consult and Strategize with Central MarComm Social Media Team Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Website Management & Digital Publishing Maintain and update website content to ensure accuracy, relevance, and timeliness. Publish daily news stories, feature content, and program-related materials. Ensure digital content is optimized for user experience, accessibility, and discoverability. Coordinate with editorial and programming staff to maintain a consistent digital presence. Percentage of time 25 Duties/Responsibilities Digital Strategy, Innovation & Revenue Support Collaborate with leadership and the Traffic Manager to explore and develop digital underwriting opportunities. Research, recommend, and implement strategies that expand audience reach and engagement. Identify emerging platforms, technologies, and content opportunities. Contribute to organizational digital growth plans and audience development initiatives. Track digital performance metrics and provide recommendations for continuous improvement. Percentage of time 5 Duties/Responsibilities Graphic Design Assist in creating graphics for new shows/events/podcasts/segments, collaborating with supervisor and central MarComm Design Team as required. Create graphics for website and social media to support programming and organizational communications. Percentage of time 5 Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Brandon Maher Recruitment Contact Email bmaher@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Documents #1 Other Documents #2 Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
