    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/498724": {
      "title": "Director for Accreditation & Institutional Effectiveness",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Director for Accreditation &amp; Institutional Effectiveness Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Director for Accreditation & Institutional Effectiveness Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S15436P Working Title Director for Accreditation & Institutional Effectiveness Department SRVPAA-SR VP Acad Affrs & Prov About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Full/Part time Full Time Work Schedule Additional Schedule Information M – F, 8 -5 pm Advertised Salary Commensurate with Experience Posting Date 07/13/2026 Open until filled Yes Closing Date Proposed Starting Date 09/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Policy Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Information Classification Title Academic Assessment Director FLSA Exempt FTE 1.00 Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a related field and 12 years of professional experience to include 3 years in a leadership role. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate preferred. 10 years of progressively responsible experience working in higher education accreditation, assessment, institutional effectiveness, academic affairs, or related administration roles. A working knowledge of accreditation and institutional effectiveness processes. Position Summary The Director for Accreditation and Institutional Effectiveness functions as the primary point of contact for campus on matters related to institutional accreditation by SACSCOC . The Director has primary responsibility for ensuring and documenting UGAs compliance with SACSCOC accreditation requirements. This includes communicating with campus regarding SACSCOC policies and procedures and working with campus leaders to develop and implement internal policies and procedures that ensure ongoing compliance. The Director oversees SACSCOC reporting requirements, including the fifth-year interim report, the decennial reaffirmation, annual reports, and substantive change notifications and approvals. The Director reports to the Chief of Staff to the Provost and supports UGA’s SACSCOC accreditation liaison. In addition, the Director plays a key role in overseeing the University’s institutional effectiveness processes. This includes the University’s strategic planning process, Academic Program Review, Support Unit Review, and Administrator Review processes. The Director also coordinates with campus offices responsible for other institutional effectiveness processes, such as unit evaluations and student learning outcomes assessment, to ensure that UGA meets SACSCOC expectations in these areas. The Director will represent and promote accreditation and institutional effectiveness priorities by serving on University and University System of Georgia committees and task forces as applicable. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Demonstrated ability to work independently, set priorities, and bring long-term projects to completion. Skill in leading collaborative initiatives with successful outcomes. Ability to gain the cooperation and assistance of faculty and staff at all levels of the University. Demonstrated ability to organize and coordinate multiple, simultaneous projects. Excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Physical Demands Traditional office environment. Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Accreditation Leadership and Compliance Serve as the primary campus resource for matters related to SACSCOC accreditation requirements, policies, procedures, and reporting. Lead university-wide planning, coordination, and documentation for reaffirmation, fifth-year interim review, annual reporting, and substantive change processes. Oversee institutional systems and processes that support ongoing compliance, including documentation of faculty and graduate student teaching credentials, academic program coordinator credentials, student achievement, and specialized accreditation activity, as applicable. Draft, review, and edit accreditation narratives, reports, and related institutional documentation. Monitor changes in accreditation requirements and emerging best practices and advise university leaders on implications for policy, process, and institutional planning. Coordinate with campus partners to develop and implement internal procedures that ensure sustained compliance with accreditation expectations. Percentage of time 45 Duties/Responsibilities Institutional Effectiveness, Planning, and Review Provide leadership for institutional effectiveness processes that support continuous improvement and demonstrate compliance with accreditation expectations. Support and coordinate university-wide strategic planning processes, including implementation monitoring, progress reporting, and committee support. Provide institutional oversight and guidance for academic program review, support unit review, and administrator review processes. Work with academic and administrative units to ensure planning, assessment, and review activities are in line with institutional and accreditation priorities and expectations. Help synthesize findings from institutional effectiveness activities for executive audiences and institutional decision-making. Percentage of time 35 Duties/Responsibilities Administrative Leadership, Campus Engagement, and Operations Supervise and support the work of the Associate Director for Accreditation and the Assistant Director for Institutional Effectiveness. Lead development and improvement of systems, tools, templates, and workflows that support accreditation and institutional effectiveness documentation and reporting. Build campus understanding of accreditation and institutional effectiveness expectations through consultation, guidance, training, and communication. Oversee the University Policy Library and provide administrative guidance for related tools and workflows in coordination with policy owners and subject matter experts. Represent accreditation and institutional effectiveness priorities on University and University System of Georgia committees, task forces, and working groups, as appropriate. Perform other related duties as assigned. Percentage of time 20 Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Maggie Parker Recruitment Contact Email mcparker@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/34131": {
      "title": "215 S. Jackson St.Athens, GA 30602Tel (706) 542-2222Email: hrweb@uga.edu",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Temporary Lab/Research Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Temporary Lab/Research Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number T00588P Working Title Temporary Lab/Research Department CAES-Applied Genetic Tech Ctr About the University of Georgia The University of Georgia ( UGA ), a land-grant and sea-grant university with statewide commitments and responsibilities is the state’s oldest, most comprehensive, and most diversified institution of higher education ( http://www.uga.edu/ ). UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA was founded in 1785 by the Georgia General Assembly as the first state-chartered University in the country. UGA employs approximately 1,800 full-time instructional faculty and more than 7,600 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 36,000 students including over 27,500 undergraduates and over 8,500 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 17 schools and colleges, as well as a medical partnership with Augusta University housed on the UGA Health Sciences Campus in Athens. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan GDCP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Non-Benefits Eligible Full/Part time Full Time Work Schedule Work Schedule (other) Monday-Friday 8am-5pm with weekend/holidays during seasonal planting and harvesting times. Advertised Salary $10.00 hr Posting Date 10/17/2018 Open until filled Yes Closing Date Proposed Starting Date 10/31/2018 Anticipated End Date Special Instructions to Applicants EEO Policy Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer.  All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, gender identity, sexual orientation or protected veteran status. Location of Vacancy Athens Area Position Information Classification Title Temporary Lab/Research Pay Grade 000 FLSA Non-Exempt FTE 100 Minimum Qualifications Minimum qualifications may be defined by the department based on the responsibilities of the position. Preferred Qualifications Position Summary A temporary/lab research position is needed to work in the soybean research lab to take agronomic notes, collect data, and harvest soybean research plots in the field. This position will work in the seed lab to weigh and clean samples, thresh individual plants, and prepare seed for spring planting. Additional Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification High school diploma Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Physical Demands The job will require lifting up to 50 lbs and overtime hours during the planting and harvesting season. Will need to be able to work in the fields and greenhouse in extreme heat. Ability to travel. Is driving required to perform essential duties outlined in this position? (This does not include infrequent trips) The successful candidate would have to provide proof that s/he has a valid driver's license when offered employment. Yes Does this position have financial responsibilities? No Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Take agronomic notes, collect data, and harvest soybean research plots in field environment. Percentage of time 45 Duties/Responsibilities Work in seed lab weighing and cleaning samples, threshing individual plants, and preparing seed for replanting in spring. Percentage of time 45 Duties/Responsibilities Greenhouse work of planting, harvesting, and cleaning. Percentage of time 10 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess a valid driver's license? No Response No Yes Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
