    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/500801": {
      "title": "Peanut Research Technician- Tifton Campus",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Peanut Research Technician- Tifton Campus Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Peanut Research Technician- Tifton Campus Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include a list of references, CV, and cover letter. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S15616P Working Title Peanut Research Technician- Tifton Campus Department CAES-Tifton Campus About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Full/Part time Full Time Work Schedule Additional Schedule Information Schedule is to be set by supervisor and may vary during harvesting season. Advertised Salary Commensurate with Experience Posting Date 08/18/2026 Open until filled Yes Closing Date Proposed Starting Date 09/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please include a list of references, CV, and cover letter. Location of Vacancy Tifton Area EEO Policy Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Information Classification Title Research Tech-Life Science II FLSA Non-Exempt FTE 1.00 Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and 2 years of related experience Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree in an agricultural related field Position Summary The Research Technician position will be under the Assistant Dean’s office based at the University of Georgia Tifton Campus; however, frequent travel to research farms and off-site locations throughout Georgia’s peanut production regions will be necessary to support breeding and variety evaluation activities. At appointment, the person in this position will assist with research that focuses on all aspects of peanut production. The primary focus of current research projects is to support peanut breeding and agronomic programs and initiatives. This position will also provide assistance, as needed, to other research areas related to peanut improvement and production. This role will involve collaborating with and assisting researchers, graduate students, technicians, and student workers to achieve program objectives and support ongoing research activities. General responsibilities will include routine field maintenance such as cultivation, spraying, fertilization, irrigation, and other crop management activities necessary for successful field research. Additional duties will include tissue sampling, data collection in field and laboratory settings, plot establishment and maintenance, plant and plot harvesting, peanut grading and shelling, seed packaging and inventory management, planting, and operation of research equipment. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Good written and verbal communication skills. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office software. Competency in calibrating sprayers, fertilizer applicators, and related math skills. Competency in crop management. Basic mechanical, welding and carpentry skills. Understanding and appreciation of the precision necessary for agricultural research. Ability to maintain research and farm implements for optimum operation. Physical Demands Lift 50 lb items repeatedly in the heat. Operate and haul farm equipment. Bend over, walk, climb, repeatedly for long hours. Work outside in dusty, hot, humid conditions all day. Driving as needed to perform job duties. Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Prepare and maintain research plots. Support routine crop management activities, including irrigation, fertilization, weed control, and other practices necessary to maintain research trials. Collect, record, and maintain research data and observations from field and greenhouse activities. Travel to support planting, maintenance, and harvesting activities at off-site research locations as needed. Percentage of time 40 Duties/Responsibilities Manage the collection, processing, evaluation, storage, and distribution of plant, seed, and other research materials. Collect samples and data from research trials and maintain accurate records to support program objectives. Operate, maintain, and calibrate laboratory, field, and specialized agricultural equipment. Coordinate seed handling activities, including harvesting, grading, shelling, packaging, inventory management, and preparation for planting. Ensure compliance with all applicable safety procedures, quality standards, and research protocols while conducting laboratory and field activities. Percentage of time 35 Duties/Responsibilities Perform routine preventative maintenance, troubleshooting, and minor repairs on research, field, and laboratory equipment. Monitor equipment performance and identify maintenance needs to minimize downtime and support efficient research operations. Maintain facilities, equipment, and work areas in a safe and organized condition. Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Other duties assigned. Percentage of time 5 Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Ismael Brown Recruitment Contact Email inbrown@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Other Documents #1 Other Documents #2 Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/503609": {
      "title": "215 S. Jackson St.Athens, GA 30602Tel (706) 542-2222Email: hrweb@uga.edu",
      "description": "University of Georgia | Building Services Worker II Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Building Services Worker II Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number S15678P Working Title Building Services Worker II Department FMD-Svcs-Blding Svcs About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state’s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University’s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University’s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The UGA Facilities Management Division is the largest of 7 divisions reporting to the Vice President for Finance and Administration. The exceptional staff of over 800 personnel manage, operate, and maintain campus landscapes, buildings, and infrastructure to promote the long-term sustainability of the University of Georgia. College/Unit/Department website https://fmd.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Full/Part time Full Time Work Schedule Additional Schedule Information Monday-Friday, 7:00 AM-4:00 PM Voluntary On call Essential Worker Some nights and/or weekends may be needed to meet the needs of the organization. Advertised Salary $38,650.00 Posting Date 08/31/2026 Open until filled Yes Closing Date Proposed Starting Date 09/30/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Policy Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Information Classification Title Building Services Worker II FLSA Non-Exempt FTE 1.00 Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and 2 years of related experience Preferred Qualifications Custodial Experience & Equipment Use Proficiency with custodial tools like vacuum cleaners, wet/dry vacuums, T-1 scrubbers, and other small machines Experience with specialized floor care equipment for tasks like carpet extraction, stripping/waxing, and refinishing wood floors Experience with floor care with large, specialized floor care equipment: carpet cleaning and extraction, strip/wax/burnish floors, refinish wood floors, etc. Soft Skills & Availability Strong communication and teamwork abilities Flexibility to work night shifts and weekends as needed Position Summary The Building Services Worker II duties are inclusive of those of the BSW I; sweeps, dust mop, wet mop, dusts, high dusts, light floor care. Cleans windows, window sills, walls, furniture, and other equipment in and around university buildings and grounds. Collects and removes bulk quantities of trash and recyclables. Secures and unlocks university buildings. Delivers, receives, and transports miscellaneous supplies and materials to and from various buildings. Performs cleaning and disinfection on surfaces such as: glass, windows, doors, electrical switches, Venetian blinds, and other building related equipment in classrooms, restrooms, administrative buildings, recreational and fitness building, laboratories, medical clinics, etc. Maintains adequate supplies in restrooms and janitorial closets. May be needed to perform bodily fluid clean-up or specialized viral/bacterial disinfection. Performs minor light bulb replacement from an 8’ ladder. In addition, the BSWII performs floor care with large specialized floor care equipment: carpet cleaning and extraction, strip / wax / burnish floors, refinish wood floors, etc. Responsible to the safe operation and operator level maintenance of assigned equipment. Responsible for building walk-through inspections on weekly basis, assist with equipment inspections of building cleaning machine and tools, and the submission of building and/or equipment inspection form to lead/supervisor. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Attitude, initiative, and interest in the job details will be considered on an equal basis with related experience. Available to work specified shift. Available to work Saturday, Sunday, or after hours as needed. Have stability in past employment. Establish and maintain effective communication and working relationships. Physical Demands Lift up to 40 lbs, push or pull custodial carts up to 40 lbs. Load and unload heavy floor care machines. Frequently bend, squat, lift, kneel, and work with hands above head Move throughout buildings to include climbing stairs and riding elevators to perform work. Work from 8’ ladders. Travel to, to include walking to, building in area of responsibility. Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Performs floor care with large specialized floor care equipment: carpet cleaning and extraction, strip / wax burnish floors, refinish wood floors, etc. Responsible to the safe operation and operator level maintenance of assigned equipment. Percentage of time 30 Duties/Responsibilities Sweeps, dusts. washes, wet / dry mops, light floor maintenance, vacuums, and performs other duties as needed to maintain cleanliness of campus floors. Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Collect and remove trash and recyclables, clean and disinfect counters, restrooms fixtures, equipment, and furnishings and performs other duties as needed to maintain the cleanliness of laboratories, office areas, classrooms, restrooms,clinics, recreational facilities, and / or assigned work areas. Percentage of time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Cleans and restocks restrooms.Ensures adequate stock of resupply items are in janitorial closets. Percentage of time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Performs bodily fluid clean-up or specialized viral / bacterial disinfection. Perform minor light bulb replacement from an 8’ ladder. Performs related responsibilities as needed. Percentage of time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Conduct walk-through area/building inspections for cleanliness, conduct cleaning equipment inspection for safety hazards, and completes inspection reports to submit to lead/supervisor. Percentage of time 10 Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Kim Faust Recruitment Contact Email kjfaust@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone 706-296-9512 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What’s your comfort level with performing minor building maintenance (e.g., bulb replacement, equipment checks)? (Open Ended Question) * Are you available to work night shifts or weekends, if needed? (Open Ended Question) * This role may involve walking long distances, climbing stairs, and working from ladders. Are you comfortable with these physical demands? (Open Ended Question) * Are you comfortable with cross training (Open Ended Question) * Are you fluent in both Spanish and English? Yes No * This position requires the ability understand and follow written and verbal instructions in English for safety, training, and job-related communications. Are you able to meet this requirement. Yes No * Do you have a valid driver's license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
