xperience working with preschool children. Position Summary The assistant teacher works with the other members of the teaching team to create a positive, productive, professional environment for the children within their classroom. The responsibilities are determined by the job description and needs of the classroom, as identified by the lead teacher and/or administrators. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Professionalism; Working knowledge of young children’s development and developmentally appropriate practice; On-going desire and pursuit of additional educational training. Physical Demands Participate in all activities with children ages birth through five which includes squatting, lifting, sitting on the floor, and standing. Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? Yes Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities The assistant teacher is responsible for aiding the lead teacher in the classroom throughout all daily activities and interactions with children. On-going supervision of children. Percentage of time 70 Duties/Responsibilities Implementation of planned activities, maintaining a safe environment, and supervision. Percentage of time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Daily assistance in food service to children and supervision during meal times. Percentage of time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Daily assistance with diapering and/or toilet training while maintaining adequate supervision during bathroom times. Percentage of time 10 Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Lori Treff Recruitment Contact Email ldtreff@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone 706-542-4924 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * Do you have an Associates Degree (or higher degree) in ECE? yes no * Write about your philosophy of educating young children and  how you approach discipline. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status