formation This position offers up to 20-hours per week. Advertised Salary $14/hour (or current Auxiliary Services student employee hourly rate, if higher). Anticipated Start Date 05/18/2026 Posting Date 03/17/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EOO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities The Auxiliary Summer Ambassador will work as part of a team alongside fellow ambassadors and staff members to support summer orientation sessions by: Engaging with new students to answer questions and facilitate discussions about Auxiliary Services Assisting in the preparation and execution of orientation activities and materials Educating attendees on the operations and benefits of Auxiliary programs on campus Introducing new students to Auxiliary Services locations and amenities Percentage of time 100 Position Details Position Information Classification Title Temporary Technical Paraprofessional FLSA Non-Exempt UGA Job Code FTE 0.47 Minimum Qualifications Position Summary The Auxiliary Summer Ambassador serves as a key representative of UGA Auxiliary Services, helping to educate first-year students, transfer students, and their supporters of its services and programs. Through summer orientation sessions, ambassadors provide essential information on Auxiliary Services, including the Bookstore, Dining Services, Golf Course, Transportation and Parking Services, and Vending Services. In this role, ambassadors actively engage with orientation visitors, support new students in their transition to campus life, and assist with major orientation events such as the Resource Fair, Orientation Breakfast and Lunch, Breakout Sessions, Presentation Sessions, and more. Additional responsibilities may include leading tours, participating in promotional events, capturing photos and videos, and contributing to digital communications efforts as needed. This position offers a unique opportunity to develop leadership, public speaking, and customer service skills while making a meaningful impact on the UGA community. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, Certification in Position Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Strong verbal communication skills and the ability to interact with a diverse audience, including students, parents, and campus visitors A positive and welcoming attitude to create an inclusive and engaging environment Excellent customer service skills with a proactive approach to assisting others Ability to work collaboratively in a team setting Physical Demands Lift, bend, stoop, squat, reach, crouch, and kneel; lifting at least 25 pounds. Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a requirement of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Contact Information Recruitment Contact Contact Details For questions concerning this position or recruitment progression, please refer to the Recruitment Contact listed below. Recruitment Contact Name Robel Negussie Recruitment Contact Email robel.negussie@uga.edu Recruitment Contact Phone Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently enrolled at the University of Georgia as a full-time student (at least 12 credit hours per semester)? yes no * Are you currently enrolled or planning to enroll for the summer (at least 6 credit hours per semester)? (Open Ended Question) * Tell us about your experience with marketing/communicating a message. (250 word max) (Open Ended Question) * How did you hear about this vacant position? \r\n(UGA Jobs -UGA's Job Board, LinkedIn, Indeed.com, Inside HigherEdJobs, UGA Staff Listserv, Terry College Listserv, a current UGA Employee, other - please provide resource) (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of Reference